WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.376 --> 00:00:03.209
(upbeat chiptune)

00:00:05.016 --> 00:00:07.118
- Strong Museum in Rochester, New York,

00:00:07.118 --> 00:00:10.755
is also know as the
National Museum of Play.

00:00:10.755 --> 00:00:14.088
More than half million objects are here.

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:19.422
My name is Chris Bench, I'm vice president

00:00:19.422 --> 00:00:23.267
for collections of the
museum and its chief curator.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.355
Our collections are divided by category

00:00:25.355 --> 00:00:27.097
and here are some of the people

00:00:27.097 --> 00:00:29.977
who are responsible for that:

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:33.560
Nicolas Ricketts is
Curator of Board Games.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.217
- In our collection, we have
around 10,000 board games

00:00:41.549 --> 00:00:44.049
and it parallels, essentially,

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.249
American History since the Revolution.

00:00:48.249 --> 00:00:50.729
When you think in terms of games,

00:00:50.729 --> 00:00:52.409
they all tend to represent the areas

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:54.067
in which they were created.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.526
It’s a different way of
getting into the mindset

00:00:56.526 --> 00:01:00.307
of people who lived a hundred years ago.

00:01:00.307 --> 00:01:04.474
- There's Michelle Parnett
Dwyer, Curator of Dolls.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:10.362
- In this collection, we
have more than 15,000 dolls

00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:14.544
and it spans from the 18th
century to present day.

00:01:14.544 --> 00:01:18.661
Dolls are special because
of the way that we connect

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:21.502
with them, we project ourselves,

00:01:21.502 --> 00:01:25.582
our hobbies, our interests,
our values towards others.

00:01:25.582 --> 00:01:28.382
When we look at the history of dolls

00:01:28.382 --> 00:01:30.480
and how we've played with them,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.936
it shows that we connect
to people from the past

00:01:33.936 --> 00:01:37.009
in ways that we might not have expected.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:39.649
- Martin Reinhardt, head of pinball

00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:41.982
and arcade game collections.

00:01:43.743 --> 00:01:45.844
- We've over 250 arcade machines

00:01:45.844 --> 00:01:49.483
and over 100 pinball
machines in the collection.

00:01:49.483 --> 00:01:53.588
Pinball is real, you can
feel the way the game plays,

00:01:53.588 --> 00:01:57.781
you can feel the way the
game moves as you're playing.

00:01:57.781 --> 00:02:01.108
It's just in my nature to
keep these machines going.

00:02:01.108 --> 00:02:03.151
They were made the last five years

00:02:03.151 --> 00:02:04.772
in a commercial environment and the fact

00:02:04.772 --> 00:02:07.405
that we have games that are 30, 40,

00:02:07.405 --> 00:02:10.238
50, 60 years old is amazing to me.

00:02:12.051 --> 00:02:16.312
- So I'm Curator responsible
for General Toys,

00:02:16.312 --> 00:02:19.083
things like action figures and yo-yos.

00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:22.833
This collection has more
than 70,000 objects.

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.139
Toys always reflect what's going on

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:28.518
in the world around them, when it's

00:02:28.518 --> 00:02:31.638
economic boom times,
construction toys are big.

00:02:31.638 --> 00:02:34.097
When US is at war, we see all

00:02:34.097 --> 00:02:37.476
sorts of military and war toys.

00:02:37.476 --> 00:02:41.117
The toy collection is a wonderful example

00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:43.418
of how times have changed and

00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:46.618
people have changed over the years.

00:02:46.618 --> 00:02:49.357
Play is really important,
it's an integral part

00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:51.658
to who we are as human beings,

00:02:51.658 --> 00:02:55.279
only by understanding
how play has stayed the same

00:02:55.279 --> 00:02:58.618
and more importantly,
changed over the years,

00:02:58.618 --> 00:03:01.772
can we understand how
we've developed as people

00:03:01.772 --> 00:03:04.410
and how we've played over the centuries.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.993
(upbeat music)

